+## The altitude lines of a capped size (Art's ruling, docs/art/relief-cap-ruling.md, and its follow-up of 2026-11-22): each line on tiny and small is
+## medium's scaled by the planet's tallest capped peak over the tallest relief on medium, World's WorldPlanetSize.linesScaleFor (1.0 where nothing is
+## capped: medium, big, huge, and every size while the cap's data row is off, so the lines are as they were, bit for bit). Rendering draws two: the
+## snow (SNOW_FROM, 6,720, is medium's 0.997 of 6,739, so the snow starts at 0.997 of the planet's own tallest capped peak) and the rocky biomes'
+## rock line (biome_look ROCK_ABOVE, the shader's lines_s). Per match: the materials are made once, and the tile ground copies them from this one.
+func _set_lines(S: SimState) -> void:
+	lines_s = WorldPlanetSize.linesScaleFor(SimField._planet(int(S.frame.seed), int(S.frame.gen))) if S.frame != null else 1.0
+	_terrain_mat.set_shader_parameter("snow_from", RenderLook.SNOW_FROM * lines_s)
+	_terrain_mat.set_shader_parameter("snow_full", RenderLook.SNOW_FULL * lines_s)
+	_terrain_mat.set_shader_parameter("lines_s", lines_s)
+
